1
00:00:01,335 --> 00:00:02,377
HEY.
HI.

2
00:00:02,419 --> 00:00:03,462
SORRY I'M LATE.

3
00:00:03,504 --> 00:00:04,839
DID I MISS ANYTHING?

4
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:07,716
WELL, JOEY STUFFING
15 OREOS IN HIS MOUTH.

5
00:00:08,843 --> 00:00:10,093
FIFTEEN?

6
00:00:10,135 --> 00:00:12,262
YOUR PERSONAL BEST. YEAH.

7
00:00:12,304 --> 00:00:13,973
( muffled ):
MM-MM.

8
00:00:16,809 --> 00:00:18,560
SO, WHERE WERE YOU?

9
00:00:18,602 --> 00:00:19,561
OH, ON A DATE.

10
00:00:19,603 --> 00:00:21,104
I MET THIS GIRL
ON THE TRAIN

11
00:00:21,146 --> 00:00:22,481
GOING TO A
MUSEUM UPSTATE.

12
00:00:22,523 --> 00:00:25,609
OH, YEAH, HOW'D
YOU MEET HER?
WHICH MUSEUM?

13
00:00:25,651 --> 00:00:27,945
NO. ANSWER HIS.

14
00:00:27,987 --> 00:00:31,156
OKAY, IT WAS JUST ME AND HER
AT THE BACK OF THE TRAIN

15
00:00:31,198 --> 00:00:34,284
AND I SAT NEAR THE DOOR
SO SHE'D HAVE TO PASS BY ME

16
00:00:34,326 --> 00:00:36,453
IF SHE WANTED TO, LIKE,
SWITCH CARS.

17
00:00:36,495 --> 00:00:38,789
SHE WAS TOTALLY AT MY MERCY.

18
00:00:38,831 --> 00:00:41,625
WERE YOU SO LATE BECAUSE YOU
WERE BURYING THIS WOMAN?

19
00:00:41,667 --> 00:00:43,002
NO, I'M GETTING BACK NOW

20
00:00:43,042 --> 00:00:44,920
BECAUSE SHE LIVES
IN POUGHKEEPSIE.

21
00:00:44,962 --> 00:00:46,213
SHE SEEMS REALLY GREAT

22
00:00:46,254 --> 00:00:48,674
BUT SHE'S, LIKE, TWO
AND A HALF HOURS AWAY.

23
00:00:48,716 --> 00:00:51,677
HOW CAN SHE BE GREAT IF
SHE'S FROM POUGHKEEPSIE?

24
00:00:53,012 --> 00:00:56,306
'KAY, THAT JOKE
WOULD'VE KILLED IN ALBANY.

25
00:00:56,348 --> 00:00:57,641
DONE.

26
00:00:57,683 --> 00:00:58,809
I DID IT.

27
00:00:58,851 --> 00:01:01,603
HUH. WHO'S STUPID NOW, HUH?

28
00:01:08,610 --> 00:01:13,490
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

29
00:01:13,532 --> 00:01:15,993
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

30
00:01:16,035 --> 00:01:18,328
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

31
00:01:18,370 --> 00:01:23,333
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

32
00:01:23,375 --> 00:01:24,877
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN YOUR DAY ♪

33
00:01:24,919 --> 00:01:28,547
♪ YOUR WEEK, YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

34
00:01:28,589 --> 00:01:31,299
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

35
00:01:31,341 --> 00:01:33,510
♪ WHEN THE RAIN
STARTS TO POUR ♪

36
00:01:33,552 --> 00:01:36,221
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

37
00:01:36,263 --> 00:01:38,682
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

38
00:01:38,724 --> 00:01:41,977
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

39
00:01:42,019 --> 00:01:48,149
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

40
00:01:52,404 --> 00:01:53,530
HEY, THEY'RE LIGHTING

41
00:01:53,572 --> 00:01:55,490
THE BIG CHRISTMAS TREE TONIGHT.

42
00:01:55,532 --> 00:01:57,743
UM, THAT PAPER'S
TWO WEEKS OLD.

43
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:02,372
ALL RIGHT, WHO KEEPS LEAVING
OLD NEWSPAPERS IN THE TRASH?

44
00:02:03,707 --> 00:02:05,793
I REALLY WANTED
TO TAKE KATHY TO THIS.

45
00:02:05,834 --> 00:02:07,377
I CAN'T BELIEVE I MISSED IT.

46
00:02:07,419 --> 00:02:08,837
HEY, YOU KNOW, AT LEAST

47
00:02:08,879 --> 00:02:11,006
YOU HAVE SOMEBODY TO
MISS THAT STUFF WITH.

48
00:02:11,048 --> 00:02:13,092
I HATE BEING ALONE
THIS TIME OF YEAR.

49
00:02:13,132 --> 00:02:15,594
NEXT THING YOU KNOW,
IT'LL BE VALENTINE'S DAY

50
00:02:15,636 --> 00:02:17,304
THEN MY BIRTHDAY,
THEN BANG--

51
00:02:17,345 --> 00:02:20,515
BEFORE YOU KNOW IT,
THEY'RE LIGHTING
THAT DAMN TREE AGAIN.

52
00:02:22,059 --> 00:02:24,019
OH, I WANT SOMEBODY.

53
00:02:27,397 --> 00:02:29,691
YOU KNOW? I WANT A MAN.

54
00:02:33,570 --> 00:02:34,989
I MEAN

55
00:02:35,030 --> 00:02:37,449
IT DOESN'T EVEN HAVE TO
BE A BIG RELATIONSHIP.

56
00:02:37,491 --> 00:02:39,493
YOU KNOW, JUST A FLING
WOULD BE GREAT.

57
00:02:39,534 --> 00:02:42,871
REALLY? I DIDN'T THINK GIRLS
EVER JUST WANTED A FLING.

58
00:02:42,913 --> 00:02:44,623
WELL, LET ME TELL
YOU SOMETHING.

59
00:02:44,665 --> 00:02:47,084
IT'S BEEN A LONG TIME
SINCE I'VE BEEN FLUNG.

60
00:02:47,126 --> 00:02:50,754
WELL, I KNOW WHAT I'M GIVING YOU
FOR CHRISTMAS.

61
00:02:52,756 --> 00:02:54,716
THERE ARE SOME NICE GUYS

62
00:02:54,758 --> 00:02:55,717
AT MY OFFICE.

63
00:02:55,759 --> 00:02:57,094
YOU WANT ME TO SET YOU UP?

64
00:02:57,136 --> 00:02:58,428
YEAH. WAIT A MINUTE.

65
00:02:58,470 --> 00:03:00,639
IT'S BEEN A LONG TIME
THAT I'VE BEEN SINGLE.

66
00:03:00,681 --> 00:03:02,891
HOW COME YOU'VE NEVER
OFFERED THIS BEFORE?

67
00:03:02,933 --> 00:03:04,601
WELL, I HAVE A GIRLFRIEND.

68
00:03:04,643 --> 00:03:06,061
I'M... I'M HAPPY.

69
00:03:06,103 --> 00:03:08,897
SO, I NO LONGER FEEL THE NEED
TO GO OUT OF MY WAY

70
00:03:08,939 --> 00:03:10,816
TO STOP OTHERS
FROM BEING HAPPY.

71
00:03:11,817 --> 00:03:12,860
OKAY.

72
00:03:12,901 --> 00:03:13,986
BUT NO ACCOUNTANTS.

73
00:03:14,028 --> 00:03:15,904
OH, AND NO ONE
FROM, LIKE, "LEGAL."

74
00:03:15,946 --> 00:03:18,281
I DON'T LIKE GUYS
WITH BORING JOBS.

75
00:03:18,323 --> 00:03:20,617
OH, AND ROSS WAS LIKE, WHAT,
A LION TAMER?

76
00:03:24,245 --> 00:03:25,372
HEY!
HEY.

77
00:03:25,413 --> 00:03:26,748
WHAT'S WRONG, MON?

78
00:03:26,790 --> 00:03:29,626
EVERYBODY AT
THE RESTAURANT
STILL HATES ME.

79
00:03:29,668 --> 00:03:31,586
I THOUGHT I WAS
MAKING HEADWAY.

80
00:03:31,628 --> 00:03:33,630
EVERYONE
WAS SMILING AT ME ALL DAY

81
00:03:33,672 --> 00:03:35,215
AND THEN I'D GET OFF WORK

82
00:03:35,256 --> 00:03:37,425
AND FIND OUT
THAT THEY WROTE THIS...

83
00:03:37,467 --> 00:03:39,136
ON MY CHEF'S HAT.

84
00:03:41,346 --> 00:03:45,350
HEY, MAYBE THEY MEANT TO WRITE
"QUIET, BITCH."

85
00:03:50,605 --> 00:03:53,108
HEY, HONEY,
WHAT'S THE MATTER?

86
00:03:53,150 --> 00:03:55,485
FINE, JUST TRYING TO BE NICE.

87
00:03:56,904 --> 00:03:58,947
I HAVE NOT BEEN PICKED ON
THIS MUCH

88
00:03:58,989 --> 00:04:00,574
SINCE I WAS IN KINDERGARTEN

89
00:04:00,615 --> 00:04:03,535
AND THEY HAD TO BRING IN SOMEONE
FROM JUNIOR HIGH

90
00:04:03,577 --> 00:04:05,079
TO DO THE SEESAW WITH ME.

91
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:07,539
( laughing )

92
00:04:07,581 --> 00:04:09,583
AW.

93
00:04:09,624 --> 00:04:12,251
THEY'RE DOING EVERYTHING
THEY CAN TO MAKE ME QUIT.

94
00:04:12,293 --> 00:04:14,004
IF IT WERE ANY OTHER JOB,
I WOULD

95
00:04:14,046 --> 00:04:15,172
BUT THIS IS SOMETHING

96
00:04:15,214 --> 00:04:17,091
I'VE BEEN WAITING FOR
MY WHOLE LIFE.

97
00:04:17,132 --> 00:04:18,466
WELL, HONEY,
YOU'RE THE BOSS.

98
00:04:18,508 --> 00:04:20,052
WHY DON'T YOU
JUST YELL AT THEM?

99
00:04:20,094 --> 00:04:21,136
OR FIRE THEM?

100
00:04:21,178 --> 00:04:23,180
I WOULD LOVE TO, BUT I CAN'T.

101
00:04:23,222 --> 00:04:25,974
YOU KNOW I'M NOT GOOD
AT CONFRONTATION.

102
00:04:26,016 --> 00:04:27,392
YOU KNOW WHAT YOU COULD DO?

103
00:04:27,434 --> 00:04:29,477
I REMEMBER READING
ABOUT THIS DIRECTOR--

104
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:31,063
I THINK IT WAS ORSON WELLES--

105
00:04:31,105 --> 00:04:33,648
WHO AT THE BEGINNING OF A MOVIE
WOULD HIRE SOMEBODY

106
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:36,193
JUST SO HE COULD FIRE THEM
IN FRONT OF EVERYBODY.

107
00:04:36,235 --> 00:04:38,237
THEN THEY WOULD ALL KNOW
WHO WAS BOSS.

108
00:04:39,947 --> 00:04:40,906
HEY, MON,
I'M NOT DOING ANYTHING.

109
00:04:40,948 --> 00:04:41,448
WHY DON'T YOU

110
00:04:41,489 --> 00:04:44,367
FIRE ME?

111
00:04:44,409 --> 00:04:45,535
THAT'S A GOOD IDEA.

112
00:04:45,577 --> 00:04:47,204
DO YOU KNOW HOW TO WAITER?

113
00:04:47,246 --> 00:04:49,248
GOOD ENOUGH TO GET FIRED.

114
00:04:49,289 --> 00:04:50,916
ALL RIGHT.

115
00:04:50,958 --> 00:04:52,000
YOU'RE HIRED.

116
00:04:52,042 --> 00:04:53,585
HEY.
OH.

117
00:04:53,627 --> 00:04:55,921
THAT MUST BE WHY I GOT FIRED
LAST WEEK.

118
00:04:55,963 --> 00:04:59,549
DOES THIS ORSON WELLES GUY
DIRECT BURGER KING COMMERCIALS?

119
00:05:04,805 --> 00:05:06,181
YES.

120
00:05:15,565 --> 00:05:16,650
I SAY, DREW

121
00:05:16,691 --> 00:05:19,194
ARE YOU SEEING ANYBODY
RIGHT NOW?

122
00:05:19,236 --> 00:05:22,114
UH, UH, I'M NOT ASKING FOR ME.
UH...

123
00:05:22,156 --> 00:05:24,116
I'M, I'M NOT, I'M NOT GAY.

124
00:05:24,158 --> 00:05:25,867
I'M NOT ASKING YOU OUT.

125
00:05:25,909 --> 00:05:27,161
I-I-I'M NOT GAY.

126
00:05:27,202 --> 00:05:29,037
I DIDN'T THINK YOU WERE GAY.

127
00:05:29,079 --> 00:05:30,413
I DO NOW.

128
00:05:33,416 --> 00:05:35,210
SEE, MY FRIEND,
MY FRIEND, RACHEL

129
00:05:35,252 --> 00:05:36,544
SHE WANTS TO BE SET UP.

130
00:05:36,586 --> 00:05:38,588
AH. I JUST GOT OUT
OF A BIG RELATIONSHIP.

131
00:05:38,630 --> 00:05:40,507
I'M NOT LOOKING
FOR ANYTHING SERIOUS.

132
00:05:40,548 --> 00:05:41,508
OH, WELL, YOU KNOW

133
00:05:41,549 --> 00:05:42,634
THAT MIGHT BE OKAY.

134
00:05:42,676 --> 00:05:44,511
EVEN IF IT WAS
JUST KIND OF A FLING

135
00:05:44,552 --> 00:05:46,471
THAT MIGHT BE ALL RIGHT
WITH RACHEL.

136
00:05:46,513 --> 00:05:47,722
WHOA, WHOA,
WHOA, WHOA.

137
00:05:47,764 --> 00:05:49,557
IS THIS "HOT RACHEL
THAT YOU TOOK

138
00:05:49,599 --> 00:05:51,226
TO THE CHRISTMAS PARTY"
RACHEL?

139
00:05:51,268 --> 00:05:53,352
OH, BY THE WAY,
THAT IS HER FULL NAME.

140
00:05:53,394 --> 00:05:54,729
OH, WOW.
I'M FREE FOR HER.

141
00:05:54,771 --> 00:05:55,730
WAIT A SECOND.

142
00:05:55,772 --> 00:05:57,065
I DIDN'T SAY
I WASN'T FREE.

143
00:05:57,107 --> 00:05:58,066
WHY DON'T WE

144
00:05:58,108 --> 00:05:59,067
TALK THIS OVER

145
00:05:59,109 --> 00:06:00,443
AT THE RANGER GAME
TOMORROW?

146
00:06:00,485 --> 00:06:01,611
HOLD ON.

147
00:06:01,653 --> 00:06:03,738
YOU KNOW, I JUST GOT
A BOX OF CUBANS.

148
00:06:03,780 --> 00:06:05,573
MAYBE I BRING 'EM
BY YOUR OFFICE

149
00:06:05,615 --> 00:06:06,574
AROUND, UH, 5:00?

150
00:06:06,616 --> 00:06:08,160
WELL, THAT'S
A LITTLE LATER

151
00:06:08,202 --> 00:06:10,245
THAN I, UH,
GENERALLY CARE TO STAY

152
00:06:10,287 --> 00:06:11,330
BUT SURE.

153
00:06:11,370 --> 00:06:12,956
MAYBE BEFORE
THE GAME

154
00:06:12,998 --> 00:06:15,792
WE CAN ENJOY SOME EIGHT-YEAR-OLD
SMALL BATCH BASIL HAYDENS.

155
00:06:15,834 --> 00:06:18,920
WELL, I DON'T REALLY KNOW
WHAT THAT IS, BUT LET'S!

156
00:06:23,675 --> 00:06:26,427
HEY, YOU GUYS, I'M WRITING
A HOLIDAY SONG FOR EVERYONE.

157
00:06:26,469 --> 00:06:27,679
DO YOU WANT TO HEAR IT?

158
00:06:27,721 --> 00:06:29,890
YEAH.
YES.

159
00:06:31,641 --> 00:06:32,684
OKAY.

160
00:06:32,726 --> 00:06:33,935
( clearing throat )

161
00:06:33,977 --> 00:06:37,438
♪ HAPPY HANUKKAH, MONICA ♪

162
00:06:39,233 --> 00:06:41,568
♪ MAY YOUR CHRISTMAS BE SNOWY,
JOEY ♪

163
00:06:42,986 --> 00:06:45,655
♪ HAPPY NEW YEAR,
CHANDLER AND ROSS ♪

164
00:06:45,697 --> 00:06:49,450
♪ SPIN THE DREIDEL, RACHEL. ♪

165
00:06:52,079 --> 00:06:53,288
PHEEBS, IT'S GREAT.

166
00:06:53,330 --> 00:06:54,539
OH, YAY.

167
00:06:54,581 --> 00:06:55,790
BUT YOU KNOW, UH

168
00:06:55,832 --> 00:06:58,626
"RACHEL" DOESN'T RHYME
WITH "DREIDEL."

169
00:06:58,668 --> 00:07:00,128
I KNOW, BUT IT'S SO HARD.

170
00:07:00,170 --> 00:07:02,339
NOTHING RHYMES
WITH YOUR STUPID NAME.

171
00:07:03,506 --> 00:07:04,591
WHAT ARE YOU

172
00:07:04,632 --> 00:07:05,884
TALKING ABOUT?

173
00:07:05,926 --> 00:07:08,845
LOTS OF THINGS
RHYME WITH RACHEL.

174
00:07:08,887 --> 00:07:11,598
BAGEL, MALE, JAIL,
BAIL, CABLE

175
00:07:11,639 --> 00:07:13,808
MAYPOLE...

176
00:07:13,850 --> 00:07:15,810
ALL GOOD. THANKS.

177
00:07:18,063 --> 00:07:19,522
DO YOU MAYBE
HAVE A NICKNAME

178
00:07:19,564 --> 00:07:21,942
THAT'S EASIER TO RHYME?

179
00:07:21,983 --> 00:07:22,734
DIDN'T YOUR DAD

180
00:07:22,776 --> 00:07:23,484
USED TO CALL
YOU "PUMPKIN?"

181
00:07:23,526 --> 00:07:25,028
OH, YEAH.
PUMPKIN? YEAH?

182
00:07:25,070 --> 00:07:28,198
BUT DID HE EVER CALL YOU, LIKE,
"BOODOLPH?"

183
00:07:31,076 --> 00:07:32,119
HELLO, CHILDREN.

184
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:33,912
( all greeting Chandler )

185
00:07:33,954 --> 00:07:37,040
HAVE I GOT
THE 50 GUYS FOR YOU!

186
00:07:37,082 --> 00:07:38,833
REALLY?

187
00:07:38,875 --> 00:07:40,794
I SHOWED THEM
THIS PICTURE OF YOU

188
00:07:40,835 --> 00:07:42,545
AND GUYS
WERE BUYING ME DRINKS

189
00:07:42,587 --> 00:07:43,713
GIVING ME STUFF.

190
00:07:43,755 --> 00:07:44,714
KNICKS TONIGHT?

191
00:07:44,756 --> 00:07:46,091
SURE.
WHERE ARE THE SEATS?

192
00:07:46,133 --> 00:07:48,218
WHEREVER. I'VE GOT, LIKE, 20.

193
00:07:50,053 --> 00:07:52,264
SO, WILL I LIKE
ANY OF THESE GUYS?

194
00:07:52,306 --> 00:07:53,472
WELL, YOU KNOW WHAT?

195
00:07:53,514 --> 00:07:54,808
I'M GOING TO, UH...

196
00:07:54,849 --> 00:07:56,017
I'M GOING TO PLAY THE FIELD
JUST A LITTLE BIT MORE.

197
00:07:56,059 --> 00:07:57,060
CHANDLER...

198
00:07:58,270 --> 00:08:01,522
GUYS ARE SIGNING OVER
THEIR 401(k)s TO ME.

199
00:08:01,564 --> 00:08:04,025
YOU WORK WITH ROBOTS?

200
00:08:08,447 --> 00:08:09,614
YES.

201
00:08:11,574 --> 00:08:13,618
OKAY, THERE IS
THIS ONE GUY, PATRICK.

202
00:08:13,660 --> 00:08:16,163
HE'S REALLY NICE,
HE'S FUNNY, HE'S A SWIMMER.

203
00:08:16,204 --> 00:08:17,622
OH, I LIKE SWIMMERS' BODIES.

204
00:08:17,664 --> 00:08:18,957
AND HIS FATHER

205
00:08:18,999 --> 00:08:21,168
INVENTED THAT MAGNETIC STRIP
ON CREDIT CARDS.

206
00:08:21,209 --> 00:08:22,961
OH! I LIKE CREDIT CARDS.

207
00:08:23,003 --> 00:08:24,379
SEE? NOT BAD

208
00:08:24,421 --> 00:08:26,131
AT THIS "FIXING UP" THING, HUH?

209
00:08:26,173 --> 00:08:27,299
SO, WHAT DOES HE DO?

210
00:08:27,341 --> 00:08:28,967
HE WORKS IN
THE FINE FOODS DIVISION.

211
00:08:29,009 --> 00:08:30,927
YOUR COMPANY HAS A
FINE FOODS DIVISION?

212
00:08:30,969 --> 00:08:32,471
IT'S A BIG COMPANY.

213
00:08:32,511 --> 00:08:33,680
I... IF YOU...

214
00:08:33,721 --> 00:08:35,098
NOW, WAIT A SECOND.

215
00:08:35,140 --> 00:08:36,933
YOU MAKE FOOD AND ROBOTS?

216
00:08:36,975 --> 00:08:38,352
NO.

217
00:08:38,393 --> 00:08:41,562
NO, THE ROBOTS
JUST WORK FOR THEM.

218
00:08:42,939 --> 00:08:45,066
ALL RIGHT,
I'M GOING TO GO TO WORK.

219
00:08:45,108 --> 00:08:47,444
DOES ANYBODY HAVE
A PROBLEM WITH THAT?

220
00:08:47,486 --> 00:08:48,778
YEAH, LADY, I DO.

221
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:50,030
I GOT

222
00:08:50,071 --> 00:08:51,281
A PROBLEM WITH THAT.

223
00:08:51,323 --> 00:08:52,324
YOU WANT A PROBLEM?

224
00:08:52,366 --> 00:08:53,658
I'LL GIVE YOU A PROBLEM.

225
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:55,952
OH, WHAT ARE YOU
GOING TO DO, FIRE ME?

226
00:08:55,994 --> 00:08:58,788
YOU BET YOUR ASS
I'M GOING TO FIRE YOU.

227
00:08:58,830 --> 00:08:59,873
SEE YOU LATER.

228
00:08:59,914 --> 00:09:00,999
THANKS.

229
00:09:05,879 --> 00:09:07,464
OH, WOW, I
SHOULD GET GOING.

230
00:09:07,506 --> 00:09:08,798
I'VE GOT A
DATE TONIGHT.

231
00:09:08,840 --> 00:09:10,133
OH, YEAH?
WITH WHO?

232
00:09:10,175 --> 00:09:12,469
YOU KNOW THAT GIRL
WHO LIVES IN POUGHKEEPSIE?

233
00:09:12,511 --> 00:09:14,971
YEAH.
NOT HER.

234
00:09:15,013 --> 00:09:16,973
YEAH, THIS IS SOMEONE ELSE I MET

235
00:09:17,015 --> 00:09:19,726
AND I-I CAN'T DECIDE
BETWEEN THE TWO OF THEM.

236
00:09:19,767 --> 00:09:21,811
YOU KNOW,
THE ONE FROM POUGHKEEPSIE

237
00:09:21,853 --> 00:09:24,481
EVEN THOUGH
SHE'S A TWO-HOUR TRAIN RIDE AWAY

238
00:09:24,523 --> 00:09:27,317
IS REALLY PRETTY, REALLY SMART,
AND A LOT OF FUN

239
00:09:27,359 --> 00:09:28,693
BUT THIS OTHER GIRL...

240
00:09:28,735 --> 00:09:30,487
WELL, SHE LIVES RIGHT UPTOWN.

241
00:09:30,529 --> 00:09:32,322
WELL, SHE'S...

242
00:09:32,364 --> 00:09:35,992
WELL, SHE'S, SHE'S
JUST AS PRETTY.

243
00:09:36,034 --> 00:09:38,537
I GUESS SHE'S SMART.

244
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:40,539
SHE'S NOT FUN.

245
00:09:42,207 --> 00:09:43,333
IF SHE'S NO FUN

246
00:09:43,375 --> 00:09:45,210
WHY DO YOU WANT
TO DATE HER AT ALL?

247
00:09:45,252 --> 00:09:46,627
WELL, I WANT TO GIVE HER
ANOTHER CHANCE, YOU KNOW?

248
00:09:46,669 --> 00:09:49,672
SHE LIVES SO CLOSE.

249
00:09:49,714 --> 00:09:52,342
AND, AT THE END OF THE DATE
THE OTHER TIME

250
00:09:52,384 --> 00:09:55,387
SHE SAID SOMETHING THAT WAS--
IF SHE WAS KIDDING--

251
00:09:55,429 --> 00:09:56,388
WAS VERY FUNNY.

252
00:09:56,430 --> 00:09:58,265
ON THE OTHER HAND

253
00:09:58,306 --> 00:10:01,268
IF SHE WASN'T KIDDING,
SHE'S NOT FUN, SHE'S STUPID

254
00:10:01,309 --> 00:10:02,602
AND KIND OF A RACIST.

255
00:10:04,396 --> 00:10:05,813
HEY.
HEY.

256
00:10:05,855 --> 00:10:07,357
HEY, MAN.

257
00:10:07,399 --> 00:10:09,984
OOH, HOW WAS YOUR FIRST DAY
WORKING AT THE RESTAURANT?

258
00:10:10,026 --> 00:10:11,236
DAMN!

259
00:10:18,159 --> 00:10:19,453
HEY.
HEY.

260
00:10:19,494 --> 00:10:21,746
OH, WHAT HAPPENED TO
YOUR FANCY CHEF JACKET?

261
00:10:21,788 --> 00:10:24,624
THEY BAKED IT.

262
00:10:24,665 --> 00:10:25,875
I CAN'T TAKE THIS
ANYMORE.

263
00:10:25,917 --> 00:10:26,751
I'M GOING
TO CALL A MEETING.

264
00:10:26,793 --> 00:10:27,919
I'M GOING TO FIRE YOU
TONIGHT.

265
00:10:27,961 --> 00:10:28,920
YOU GOT IT.

266
00:10:28,962 --> 00:10:29,963
OH, OH!

267
00:10:30,004 --> 00:10:31,005
WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

268
00:10:31,047 --> 00:10:32,924
YOU'RE STILL A TINY
BIT ON FIRE THERE.

269
00:10:32,966 --> 00:10:34,259
OH, THANKS.

270
00:10:34,301 --> 00:10:36,219
LISTEN, I THINK YOU GOT IT.

271
00:10:41,057 --> 00:10:42,559
OH, CHANDLER!

272
00:10:42,601 --> 00:10:45,186
YOU HAVE THE BEST
TASTE IN MEN.

273
00:10:45,228 --> 00:10:47,730
WELL, LIKE FATHER, LIKE SON.

274
00:10:49,399 --> 00:10:51,818
PATRICK AND I HAD SUCH
A GREAT TIME LAST NIGHT.

275
00:10:51,859 --> 00:10:52,944
I MEAN, I THINK THIS

276
00:10:52,986 --> 00:10:54,988
COULD TURN INTO
SOMETHING SERIOUS.

277
00:10:55,029 --> 00:10:56,948
REALLY? I THOUGHT
YOU WEREN'T EVEN LOOKING

278
00:10:56,990 --> 00:10:58,283
FOR SOMETHING SERIOUS.

279
00:10:58,325 --> 00:10:59,576
I THOUGHT YOU WERE LOOKING
FOR SOME KIND OF A FLING.

280
00:10:59,618 --> 00:11:01,453
WELL, YOU KNOW, POSSIBLY.

281
00:11:04,372 --> 00:11:07,834
YOU DIDN'T... TELL HIM
THAT, THOUGH... RIGHT?

282
00:11:07,875 --> 00:11:09,961
W'UH...

283
00:11:10,003 --> 00:11:11,754
NO?

284
00:11:11,796 --> 00:11:15,008
YOU TOLD THIS GUY THAT I
WAS LOOKING FOR A FLING?!

285
00:11:15,049 --> 00:11:18,345
YOU DON'T TELL THE GUY THAT!

286
00:11:18,386 --> 00:11:19,513
I'D BE THRILLED
IF I HEARD

287
00:11:19,554 --> 00:11:20,514
THAT SOME HOT GIRL
WAS JUST LOOKING TO GET...

288
00:11:20,555 --> 00:11:22,015
OH, I SEE.

289
00:11:22,056 --> 00:11:24,809
OH! BETWEEN YOU TELLING HIM
I WANTED TO HAVE A FLING

290
00:11:24,851 --> 00:11:26,894
AND ME PUTTING OUT
ON THE FIRST DATE

291
00:11:26,936 --> 00:11:29,356
OH, HE'S SO GOING TO
GET THE WRONG IDEA!

292
00:11:33,943 --> 00:11:35,778
JOEY, COULD YOU PASS
THE CHEESE?

293
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:37,405
YEAH. LISTEN,
I'D PREFER IT

294
00:11:37,447 --> 00:11:39,824
IF YOU WOULDN'T

295
00:11:39,866 --> 00:11:40,783
CALL ME JOEY.

296
00:11:40,825 --> 00:11:41,700
SINCE I DON'T
KNOW ANYONE HERE

297
00:11:41,742 --> 00:11:42,619
I THOUGHT IT MIGHT BE FUN

298
00:11:42,661 --> 00:11:44,037
TO TRY OUT A COOL
WORK NICKNAME.

299
00:11:44,078 --> 00:11:45,121
HEY, DRAGON.

300
00:11:46,623 --> 00:11:49,584
HERE'S YOUR TIPS FROM
MONDAY AND TUESDAY.

301
00:11:49,626 --> 00:11:53,421
OH. LOOKS LIKE THERE'S, LIKE,
300 BUCKS IN THIS ONE.

302
00:11:53,463 --> 00:11:55,089
YEAH, PEOPLE GET
PRETTY GENEROUS

303
00:11:55,131 --> 00:11:56,383
AROUND THE HOLIDAYS.

304
00:11:56,424 --> 00:11:58,552
AND IT NEVER HURTS TO
WEAR TIGHT TROUSERS.

305
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:01,888
OKAY.

306
00:12:01,929 --> 00:12:03,598
WOULD THE WAITERS
GATHER 'ROUND

307
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:05,099
TO HEAR
TONIGHT'S SPECIALS?

308
00:12:05,141 --> 00:12:06,934
FIRST, THERE'S
A CHILEAN SEA BASS

309
00:12:06,976 --> 00:12:09,229
PREPARED WITH A MANGO RELISH
ON A BED...

310
00:12:09,270 --> 00:12:11,439
WHY IS NOBODY
WRITING THESE DOWN?

311
00:12:11,481 --> 00:12:13,024
BECAUSE WE CAN
REMEMBER THEM.

312
00:12:13,066 --> 00:12:14,733
AND BECAUSE YOU'RE ALL GOING
TO MAKE UP FAKE SPECIALS

313
00:12:14,775 --> 00:12:15,569
AND MAKE ME COOK THEM

314
00:12:15,610 --> 00:12:17,696
LIKE YOU DID
THE OTHER NIGHT?

315
00:12:17,736 --> 00:12:20,948
WELL, SURE, THAT, TOO.

316
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:24,077
OKAY. FORGET THE SPECIALS
FOR A MINUTE.

317
00:12:24,118 --> 00:12:26,621
UM, ALL RIGHT,
HERE'S THE THING.

318
00:12:26,663 --> 00:12:29,957
FOR THE LAST TWO WEEKS,
I HAVE, UH...

319
00:12:29,999 --> 00:12:34,462
TRIED REALLY HARD TO CREATE
A POSITIVE ATMOSPHERE.

320
00:12:34,504 --> 00:12:36,172
CAN'T HEAR YOU.

321
00:12:38,007 --> 00:12:40,009
A POSITIVE
ATMOSPHERE...

322
00:12:40,051 --> 00:12:42,345
BUT I-I'VE HAD IT UP TO HERE.

323
00:12:46,349 --> 00:12:50,228
FROM NOW ON,
IT IS GOING TO BE MY WAY...

324
00:12:50,270 --> 00:12:53,981
OR THE HIGHWAY, ALL RIGHT?

325
00:12:54,023 --> 00:12:57,694
DOES ANYBODY
HAVE A PROBLEM WITH THAT?

326
00:13:05,201 --> 00:13:07,120
HEY, NEW GUY?

327
00:13:07,161 --> 00:13:09,163
I SAID...

328
00:13:09,205 --> 00:13:11,874
DOES ANYBODY HAVE A PROBLEM
WITH THAT?

329
00:13:13,167 --> 00:13:15,044
NO, MA'AM.

330
00:13:16,630 --> 00:13:18,047
HEY, HE HAS A NAME.

331
00:13:18,089 --> 00:13:19,257
IT'S DRAGON.

332
00:13:20,841 --> 00:13:22,469
YOU WANT TO KNOW
YOUR NAME?

333
00:13:22,510 --> 00:13:24,011
CHECK YOUR HAT.

334
00:13:24,053 --> 00:13:25,555
WE DID THE HAT, RIGHT?

335
00:13:31,478 --> 00:13:34,021
WHAT HAPPENED?
I AM SO SORRY.

336
00:13:34,063 --> 00:13:35,856
I WAS GOING
TO DO IT. REALLY.

337
00:13:35,898 --> 00:13:37,442
BUT THEN I WAS
STANDING THERE

338
00:13:37,484 --> 00:13:39,527
WITH $327 IN ONE HAND

339
00:13:39,569 --> 00:13:41,404
AND $238
IN THE OTHER HAND

340
00:13:41,446 --> 00:13:43,030
AND I WAS THINKING, "WOW.

341
00:13:43,072 --> 00:13:46,785
IT'S BEEN A LONG TIME
SINCE I HAD..."

342
00:13:46,825 --> 00:13:49,788
327 PLUS $238.

343
00:13:49,828 --> 00:13:51,706
JOEY, WE HAD A DEAL.

344
00:13:51,748 --> 00:13:53,374
THAT'S WHY YOU'RE HERE.

345
00:13:53,416 --> 00:13:54,875
I'VE GOT TO FIRE YOU.

346
00:13:54,917 --> 00:13:56,628
AND I'VE GOT TO PAY RENT.

347
00:13:56,670 --> 00:13:58,171
( sighs )

348
00:13:58,212 --> 00:13:59,380
LOOK

349
00:13:59,422 --> 00:14:00,548
HOW ABOUT THIS?

350
00:14:00,590 --> 00:14:01,800
YOU DON'T FIRE ME.

351
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:03,842
INSTEAD, I STAY HERE,
I GAIN THEIR TRUST

352
00:14:03,884 --> 00:14:06,513
AND THEY'LL START LISTENING
TO ALL THE NICE THINGS

353
00:14:06,554 --> 00:14:08,139
I'VE BEEN SAYING ABOUT YOU.

354
00:14:08,181 --> 00:14:10,725
WHAT KIND OF THINGS
YOU BEEN SAYING?

355
00:14:10,767 --> 00:14:11,850
NOTHING YET.

356
00:14:11,892 --> 00:14:13,770
THEY REALLY HATE YOU
AND I WANT TO FIT IN.

357
00:14:15,104 --> 00:14:16,606
♪ HAPPY, HAPPY HANUKKAH ♪

358
00:14:16,648 --> 00:14:18,024
♪ CHANDLER AND MONICA ♪

359
00:14:18,065 --> 00:14:19,233
♪ MERRY, MERRY... ♪

360
00:14:19,275 --> 00:14:21,486
OOH, YOU KNOW...
YOU KNOW WHAT, PHEEBS?

361
00:14:21,528 --> 00:14:24,030
I'M NOT JEWISH, SO...

362
00:14:24,071 --> 00:14:27,074
SO ROSS DOESN'T REALLY
DECORATE HIS TREE WITH FLOSS

363
00:14:27,116 --> 00:14:29,910
BUT YOU DON'T HEAR HIM
COMPLAINING, DO YOU? GOD!

364
00:14:29,952 --> 00:14:31,496
( yells out )

365
00:14:31,538 --> 00:14:33,540
WHAT?

366
00:14:33,581 --> 00:14:34,708
BAD DREAM?

367
00:14:35,750 --> 00:14:37,377
I WASN'T SLEEPING.

368
00:14:37,418 --> 00:14:39,086
OH, YEAH?

369
00:14:39,128 --> 00:14:41,088
THEN WHAT WAS
PHOEBE'S SONG ABOUT?

370
00:14:41,130 --> 00:14:44,008
THE ONE WITH THE CAT.

371
00:14:45,468 --> 00:14:47,554
I GOT TO GO.

372
00:14:47,595 --> 00:14:49,806
I GOT ANOTHER DATE.

373
00:14:49,848 --> 00:14:51,766
OH, SO DID YOU
PICK ONE YET?

374
00:14:51,808 --> 00:14:53,393
NO.

375
00:14:53,434 --> 00:14:55,854
IT TURNS OUT THE ONE FROM UPTOWN
WAS MAKING A JOKE

376
00:14:55,895 --> 00:14:58,105
BUT IT WAS A DIFFERENT JOKE
THAN I THOUGHT.

377
00:14:58,147 --> 00:14:59,315
IT WASN'T THAT FUNNY.

378
00:15:01,108 --> 00:15:02,819
SO I'M STILL TORN.

379
00:15:02,861 --> 00:15:04,654
YOU DON'T REALLY LIKE
THE ONE UPTOWN

380
00:15:04,696 --> 00:15:07,782
AND YOU'RE TOO EXHAUSTED FROM
DATING THE ONE IN POUGHKEEPSIE

381
00:15:07,824 --> 00:15:09,409
SO I SAY YOU END THEM BOTH.

382
00:15:09,450 --> 00:15:12,203
TAKE A TRAIN UP TO POUGHKEEPSIE
AND YOU BREAK UP WITH HER

383
00:15:12,245 --> 00:15:14,622
AND ON YOUR WAY BACK,
YOU BREAK UP WITH UPTOWN

384
00:15:14,664 --> 00:15:16,750
AND THEN BY THE TIME
YOU GET HOME TONIGHT

385
00:15:16,791 --> 00:15:18,000
YOU'RE DONE.

386
00:15:18,042 --> 00:15:19,878
YOU KNOW WHAT, YOU'RE RIGHT.

387
00:15:19,919 --> 00:15:21,421
THANK YOU.

388
00:15:21,462 --> 00:15:24,799
YEAH. I HAD A SIMILAR PROBLEM
WHEN I LIVED IN PRAGUE.

389
00:15:26,092 --> 00:15:27,134
PRAGUE?

390
00:15:27,176 --> 00:15:29,679
SO MUCH YOU DON'T KNOW.

391
00:15:39,731 --> 00:15:40,815
( slams )

392
00:15:40,857 --> 00:15:41,982
( thuds )

393
00:15:42,817 --> 00:15:44,068
CHANDLER

394
00:15:44,110 --> 00:15:46,987
PATRICK JUST ENDED
THINGS WITH ME.

395
00:15:47,029 --> 00:15:48,782
DID YOU OR DID YOU
NOT TELL HIM

396
00:15:48,823 --> 00:15:52,326
THAT I WAS LOOKING FOR
A SERIOUS RELATIONSHIP?

397
00:15:52,368 --> 00:15:54,245
I DID! I ABSOLUTELY DID!

398
00:15:54,287 --> 00:15:56,247
YOU IDIOT!

399
00:15:56,289 --> 00:15:58,958
I'M SURE YOU'RE RIGHT,
BUT WHY?

400
00:15:58,999 --> 00:16:00,376
YOU DON'T TELL A GUY

401
00:16:00,418 --> 00:16:03,045
THAT YOU'RE LOOKING FOR
A SERIOUS RELATIONSHIP.

402
00:16:03,087 --> 00:16:04,798
YOU DON'T TELL
THE GUY THAT!

403
00:16:04,839 --> 00:16:06,340
NOW YOU SCARED HIM AWAY.

404
00:16:06,382 --> 00:16:07,675
OH, MAN.
I AM SORRY.

405
00:16:07,717 --> 00:16:09,302
I AM SO, SO SORRY.

406
00:16:09,343 --> 00:16:12,597
YOU KNOW, YOU SHOULD NEVER
BE ALLOWED TO TALK TO PEOPLE.

407
00:16:12,639 --> 00:16:15,057
I KNOW! I KNOW!

408
00:16:15,099 --> 00:16:18,352
NOW I'M RIGHT BACK
WHERE I STARTED.

409
00:16:18,394 --> 00:16:19,896
OH, THIS SUCKS.

410
00:16:19,938 --> 00:16:22,356
BEING ALONE SUCKS!

411
00:16:22,398 --> 00:16:23,399
YOU KNOW WHAT?

412
00:16:23,441 --> 00:16:24,943
YOU'RE GOING TO MEET SOMEBODY.

413
00:16:24,983 --> 00:16:27,069
YOU'RE
A GREAT CATCH.

414
00:16:27,111 --> 00:16:29,405
WHEN I WAS TELLING
ALL THOSE GUYS ABOUT YOU

415
00:16:29,447 --> 00:16:31,616
I DIDN'T HAVE TO LIE ONCE.

416
00:16:32,784 --> 00:16:34,034
REALLY?

417
00:16:34,076 --> 00:16:35,620
YEAH.

418
00:16:35,662 --> 00:16:39,248
YOU GRADUATED
MAGNA CUM LAUDE, RIGHT?

419
00:16:39,290 --> 00:16:40,750
NO.

420
00:16:40,792 --> 00:16:42,460
AW, IT DOESN'T MATTER.

421
00:16:44,838 --> 00:16:46,130
HEY, YOU KNOW WHAT?

422
00:16:46,172 --> 00:16:47,465
I GOT TWO TICKETS
TO TONIGHT'S RANGER GAME.

423
00:16:47,507 --> 00:16:49,509
YOU WANT
TO COME WITH ME?

424
00:16:50,050 --> 00:16:52,428
CUTE GUYS
IN LITTLE SHORTS?

425
00:16:52,470 --> 00:16:54,722
SURE.

426
00:16:54,764 --> 00:16:56,599
WELL, ACTUALLY,
IT'S A HOCKEY TEAM

427
00:16:56,641 --> 00:16:58,643
SO IT'S ANGRY CANADIANS
WITH NO TEETH.

428
00:16:58,685 --> 00:17:01,228
WELL, THAT SOUNDS FUN, TOO.

429
00:17:01,270 --> 00:17:02,814
THANK YOU.

430
00:17:02,856 --> 00:17:04,607
OKAY.

431
00:17:07,735 --> 00:17:11,113
HAVE YOU EVER BEEN
WITH A WOMAN?

432
00:17:11,155 --> 00:17:13,031
WHAT?

433
00:17:13,073 --> 00:17:15,702
CHANDLER, WHAT IS
THE MATTER WITH YOU?

434
00:17:15,743 --> 00:17:19,372
SO THERE IS NO GOOD TIME
TO ASK THAT QUESTION.

435
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:24,794
THE STATION IS POUGHKEEPSIE.

436
00:17:24,836 --> 00:17:26,546
POUGHKEEPSIE.

437
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:29,883
ROSS?

438
00:17:29,924 --> 00:17:32,218
ROSS?

439
00:17:32,259 --> 00:17:33,386
WAKE UP.

440
00:17:33,427 --> 00:17:34,971
ROSS?

441
00:17:35,013 --> 00:17:37,682
ROS... ROSS!

442
00:17:37,724 --> 00:17:39,851
ROSS! ROSS!

443
00:17:43,021 --> 00:17:44,939
I NEED MORE SWORDFISH.

444
00:17:44,981 --> 00:17:47,274
CAN YOU GET ME
SOME MORE SWORDFISH?

445
00:17:47,316 --> 00:17:49,485
I DON'T SPEAK ENGLISH.

446
00:17:49,527 --> 00:17:51,612
YOU DID A MINUTE AGO.

447
00:17:51,654 --> 00:17:53,698
WELL, I DON'T KNOW
WHAT TO TELL YA.

448
00:17:55,408 --> 00:17:56,868
FINE.

449
00:18:05,543 --> 00:18:08,629
OKAY, VERY FUNNY.

450
00:18:08,671 --> 00:18:11,173
( banging ):
CAN SOMEBODY
LET ME OUT, PLEASE?

451
00:18:11,215 --> 00:18:13,760
COME ON, I'M COLD!

452
00:18:13,801 --> 00:18:16,012
( clattering pans )

453
00:18:16,054 --> 00:18:18,056
AND COVERED
IN MARINARA SAUCE!

454
00:18:18,097 --> 00:18:20,558
( banging ):
COME ON, LET ME OUT!

455
00:18:24,395 --> 00:18:27,523
YOU FOUND THAT HANDLE,
DID YA?

456
00:18:27,565 --> 00:18:29,525
THAT'S NOT FUNNY.

457
00:18:29,567 --> 00:18:32,028
WELL, THAT'S NOT TRUE.

458
00:18:34,072 --> 00:18:35,865
I'M A GOOD PERSON

459
00:18:35,907 --> 00:18:37,450
AND I'M A GOOD CHEF

460
00:18:37,491 --> 00:18:40,244
AND I DON'T DESERVE TO HAVE
MARINARA SAUCE ALL OVER ME.

461
00:18:41,913 --> 00:18:43,497
IF YOU WANT ME
TO QUIT THIS BAD

462
00:18:43,539 --> 00:18:44,707
ALL YOU HAVE TO...

463
00:18:44,749 --> 00:18:46,667
HEY! CHEF GELLER.

464
00:18:46,709 --> 00:18:49,587
YOU KNOW THAT LITTLE SPEECH
YOU MADE THE OTHER DAY?

465
00:18:49,629 --> 00:18:52,632
WELL, I GOT A PROBLEM WITH IT.

466
00:18:54,050 --> 00:18:55,217
YOU DO?

467
00:18:55,259 --> 00:18:56,844
YOU BET I DO.

468
00:18:56,886 --> 00:18:59,346
I JUST, UH...

469
00:18:59,388 --> 00:19:01,557
WASN'T LISTENING THEN,
IS ALL.

470
00:19:01,599 --> 00:19:05,227
WELL, IF YOU WANT A PROBLEM

471
00:19:05,269 --> 00:19:07,105
I'LL GIVE YOU A PROBLEM.

472
00:19:07,146 --> 00:19:10,316
WHAT ARE YOU GOING TO DO,
FIRE ME?

473
00:19:10,357 --> 00:19:12,485
YOU BET YOUR ASS
I'M GOING TO FIRE YOU.

474
00:19:12,526 --> 00:19:14,153
NOW, GET OUT OF MY KITCHEN!

475
00:19:14,194 --> 00:19:15,446
GET OUT!

476
00:19:19,784 --> 00:19:21,119
ALL RIGHT

477
00:19:21,159 --> 00:19:23,830
ANYBODY ELSE
GOT A PROBLEM?

478
00:19:23,871 --> 00:19:25,999
HOW ABOUT YOU, CHUCKLES?

479
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:28,042
YOU THINK THIS IS FUNNY NOW?

480
00:19:28,084 --> 00:19:29,251
NO.

481
00:19:29,293 --> 00:19:31,129
HOW ABOUT IF DANCE AROUND

482
00:19:31,169 --> 00:19:33,047
ALL COVERED IN SAUCE, HUH?

483
00:19:33,089 --> 00:19:34,882
YOU THINK IT'S FUNNY NOW?

484
00:19:34,924 --> 00:19:37,593
NO. IT'S REALLY GOOD.

485
00:19:37,635 --> 00:19:39,219
GOOD.

486
00:19:39,261 --> 00:19:41,639
NOW, TAKE THOSE SALADS
TO TABLE FOUR

487
00:19:41,681 --> 00:19:43,683
AND YOU,
GET THE SWORDFISH

488
00:19:43,724 --> 00:19:45,267
AND YOU--

489
00:19:45,309 --> 00:19:47,269
GET A HAIRCUT.

490
00:19:50,314 --> 00:19:52,025
LAST STOP, MONTREAL.

491
00:19:52,066 --> 00:19:54,944
THE STOP IS MONTREAL.

492
00:19:57,488 --> 00:19:59,615
WHAT?

493
00:20:03,494 --> 00:20:06,873
I MADE A BET WITH MYSELF
THAT YOU HAD BEAUTIFUL EYES.

494
00:20:06,914 --> 00:20:09,834
NOW THAT I SEE THEM, I WIN.

495
00:20:12,586 --> 00:20:14,922
WHAT?

496
00:20:14,964 --> 00:20:16,590
WE'RE AT MY STOP

497
00:20:16,632 --> 00:20:18,509
BUT WOULD YOU LIKE
TO HAVE COFFEE?

498
00:20:22,429 --> 00:20:24,473
ARE WE REALLY IN MONTREAL?

499
00:20:24,515 --> 00:20:26,350
YES, WE ARE.

500
00:20:26,392 --> 00:20:27,810
SO, COFFEE?

501
00:20:29,645 --> 00:20:31,522
COFFEE SOUNDS GREAT.

502
00:20:33,983 --> 00:20:37,611
WAIT. SO, YOU LIVE
IN MONTREAL?

503
00:20:37,653 --> 00:20:40,740
NO, BUT IT'S JUST A TWO-HOUR
FERRY RIDE TO NOVA SCOTIA.

504
00:20:44,952 --> 00:20:48,122
( loudly ):
WELL, I SHOULD HAVE THOUGHT
ABOUT MY WIFE AND KIDS

505
00:20:48,164 --> 00:20:50,166
BEFORE I TALKED BACK
TO CHEF GELLER.

506
00:20:51,333 --> 00:20:52,710
( quietly ):
THANKS.

507
00:20:52,752 --> 00:20:55,295
YEP, LOOKS LIKE IT'S GOING
TO BE A LEAN CHRISTMAS

508
00:20:55,337 --> 00:20:57,048
AT THE DRAGON HOUSE
THIS YEAR.

509
00:20:59,175 --> 00:21:00,384
ENOUGH.

510
00:21:02,136 --> 00:21:05,056
LEAN, LEAN, LEAN.

511
00:21:08,601 --> 00:21:11,353
♪ WENT TO THE STORE,
SAT ON SANTA'S LAP ♪

512
00:21:11,395 --> 00:21:15,066
♪ ASKED HIM TO BRING MY FRIENDS
ALL KINDS OF CRAP ♪

513
00:21:15,108 --> 00:21:18,861
♪ HE SAID ALL YOU NEED
IS TO WRITE THEM A SONG ♪

514
00:21:18,903 --> 00:21:23,574
♪ THEY HAVEN'T HEARD IT YET
SO DON'T TRY TO SING ALONG ♪

515
00:21:23,616 --> 00:21:26,493
♪ NO, DON'T SING ALONG ♪

516
00:21:26,535 --> 00:21:29,580
♪ MONICA, MONICA ♪

517
00:21:29,622 --> 00:21:34,210
♪ HAVE A HAPPY HANUKKAH ♪

518
00:21:34,252 --> 00:21:37,130
♪ SAW SANTA CLAUS ♪

519
00:21:37,171 --> 00:21:39,799
♪ HE SAID HELLO TO ROSS ♪

520
00:21:39,840 --> 00:21:42,009
( strumming )

521
00:21:42,051 --> 00:21:44,845
♪ AND PLEASE TELL JOEY ♪

522
00:21:44,887 --> 00:21:49,600
♪ CHRISTMAS WILL BE SNOWY... ♪

523
00:21:49,642 --> 00:21:52,937
♪ AND RACHEL AND CHANDLER ♪

524
00:21:52,979 --> 00:21:57,691
♪ HAS A...( mumbles ) HANDLER. ♪

525
00:21:57,733 --> 00:22:01,487
[Captioned by
The Caption Center
WGBH Educational Foundation]

